{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "BSB",
  "book_code": "PRO",
  "chapter": 7,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My son, keep my words and treasure my commandments within you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Keep my commandments and live; guard my teachings as the apple of your eye.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Tie them to your fingers; write them on the tablet of your heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say to wisdom, “You are my sister,” and call understanding your kinsman,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "that they may keep you from the adulteress, from the stranger with seductive words.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For at the window of my house I looked through the lattice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I saw among the simple, I noticed among the youths, a young man lacking judgment,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "crossing the street near her corner, strolling down the road to her house,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "at twilight, as the day was fading into the dark of the night.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then a woman came out to meet him, with the attire of a harlot and cunning of heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She is loud and defiant; her feet do not remain at home.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now in the street, now in the squares, she lurks at every corner.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "She seizes him and kisses him; she brazenly says to him:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "“I have made my peace offerings; today I have paid my vows.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So I came out to meet you; I sought you, and I have found you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have decked my bed with coverings, with colored linen from Egypt.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I have perfumed my bed with myrrh, with aloes, and with cinnamon.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, let us take our fill of love till morning. Let us delight in loving caresses!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For my husband is not at home; he has gone on a long journey.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He took with him a bag of money and will not return till the moon is full.”",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "With her great persuasion she entices him; with her flattering lips she lures him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He follows her on impulse, like an ox going to the slaughter, like a deer bounding into a trap,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "until an arrow pierces his liver, like a bird darting into a snare— not knowing it will cost him his life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now, my sons, listen to me, and attend to the words of my mouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Do not let your heart turn aside to her ways; do not stray into her paths.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For she has brought many down to death; her slain are many in number.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PRO.7.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "BSB:PRO.7.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Her house is the road to Sheol, descending to the chambers of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
